 $q$mcq$q$, $q$beginner$q$,
 $q$A start-up pays each month only for the compute it actually used and bought no servers. Which cost model is this?$q$,
 $q$[{"id": "a", "text": "Consumption-based"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Capital expenditure (CapEx)", "why_wrong": "CapEx means buying assets upfront."}, {"id": "c", "text": "Perpetual licensing", "why_wrong": "That is a one-time purchase, not usage billing."}, {"id": "d", "text": "Fixed-price hosting", "why_wrong": "Fixed price ignores actual usage."}]$q$::jsonb, $q$["a"]$q$::jsonb,
 $q$With the consumption-based model you pay for what you use, which turns upfront CapEx into ongoing operating cost.$q$, $q$Microsoft Learn AZ-900 skills outline$q$),
